## Quickstart

### 1. Environment and dependencies

Install dependencies using `uv`:

```bash
uv sync
```

Copy the environment example:

```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

{% if sql_engine == 'duckdb' %}
### 2. Run dbt transformations (DuckDB)

```bash
# Parse project models and configs
uv run dbt parse --project-dir dbt --profiles-dir dbt

# Seed reference data (model registry)
uv run dbt seed --project-dir dbt --profiles-dir dbt

# Execute transformation models
uv run dbt run --project-dir dbt --profiles-dir dbt

# Execute integrity tests
uv run dbt test --project-dir dbt --profiles-dir dbt
```

### 3. Export analytical marts to Parquet

```bash
uv run python scripts/export_parquet.py
```
{% elif sql_engine == 'bigquery' %}
### 2. Run dbt transformations (BigQuery)

Ensure `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS` or `gcloud auth application-default login` is configured:

```bash
# Parse project models and configs
uv run dbt parse --project-dir dbt --profiles-dir dbt

# Execute transformation models
uv run dbt run --project-dir dbt --profiles-dir dbt

# Execute integrity tests
uv run dbt test --project-dir dbt --profiles-dir dbt
```

### 3. Export analytical marts to Parquet

```bash
uv run python scripts/export_parquet.py
```
{% endif %}

### 4. Computational manuscript

Render the Quarto manuscript:

```bash
quarto render manuscript
```
